entries.definition_en:
A man of the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.8.30; 
 son of: Abiel (H0022) and Maacah (H4601N); 
 brother of: Kish (H7027), Ner (H5369), Abdon (H5658J), Zur (H6698I), Nadab (H5070J), Gedor (H1446I), Ahio (H0283I), Zecher (H2144) and Mikloth (H4732)
 § Baal = "lord"

A man of the tribe of Reuben living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.5.5; 
 son of: Reaiah (H7211); 
 father of: Beerah (H0880)
 § Baal = "lord"

A man of the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.21; 
 son of: Benjamin (H1144); 
 brother of: Bela (H1106A), Becher (H1071), Ashbel (H0788), Naaman (H5283), Ehi (H0278), Rosh (H7220), Muppim (H4649), Huppim (H2650H), Ard (H0714), Ahiram (H0297) and Jediael (H3043); 
 father of: Ehud (H0164)
 § Gera = "a grain"
1) a son of Benjamin
2) a son of Bela and grandson of Benjamin
3) any member of the Gera family of the Benjamite tribe

A man of the tribe of Benjamin living before Israel's Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.7; 
 son of: Ehud (H0164); 
 brother of: Naaman (H5283J), Ahijah (H0281K), Uzza (H5798H) and Ahihud (H0284); also called Heglam (KJV: "removed"; NIV: "deported") at 1Ch.8.7; 
Also named: ga.lah (הֶגְלָם "Heglam" H1540)
 § Gera = "a grain"
1) a son of Benjamin
2) a son of Bela and grandson of Benjamin
3) any member of the Gera family of the Benjamite tribe

A woman of the tribe of Manasseh living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Num.26.33; 
 daughter of: Zelophehad (H6765); 
 sister of: Mahlah (H4244), Noah (H5270), Milcah (H4435H) and Tirzah (H8656) 
 § Hoglah = "partridge"
 3rd of 5 daughters of Zelophehad, a descendant of Manasseh

A man of the tribe of Asher living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.7.34; 
 son of: Shomer (H7763H); 
 brother of: Rohgah (H7303), Jehubbah (H3160) and Aram (H0758J); also translated "brother"; 
 § Ahi = "my brother"
1) a head of the families of Gad
2) an Asherite

A man of the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.8.35; 
 son of: Micah (H4318H); 
 brother of: Pithon (H6377), Tarea (H8390) and Ahaz (H0271H) 
 § Melech = "king"
 a Benjamite, the 2nd son of Micah and grandson of Mephibosheth

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, only mentioned at Gen.22.24; 
 son of: Nahor (H5152H) and Reumah (H7208); 
 brother of: Tebah (H2875), Gaham (H1514) and Tahash (H8477); 
 half-brother of: Uz (H5780H), Buz (H0938), Kemuel (H7055), Chesed (H3777), Hazo (H2375), Pildash (H6394), Jidlaph (H3044) and Bethuel (H1328A)
 § Maachah = "oppression"
son of Nahor by concubine Reumah

A woman living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.3.3; 
 daughter of: Talmai (H8526H); married to David (H1732); 
 mother of: Absalom (H0053)
 § Maachah = "oppression"
daughter of king Talmai of Geshur, wife or David, and mother of Absalom

A woman of the tribe of Judah living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ki.15.2; 
 daughter of: Uriel (H0222I) and Tamar (H8559I); married to Rehoboam (H7346); 
 mother of: Abijah (H0029I), Attai (H6262I), Ziza (H2124H) and Shelomith (H8019G); also called Micaiah (KJV: Michaiah) at 2Ch.13.2;
 § Maachah = "oppression"
daughter of Absalom, wife of king Rehoboam of Judah, and mother of king Abijam of Judah

A woman of the tribe of Manasseh living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at 1Ch.7.15; 
 daughter of: Ir (H5893G); 
 sister of: Shuppim (H8206G) and Huppim (H2650G); married to Machir (H4353G); 
 mother of: Peresh (H6570), Sheresh (H8329)
 § Maachah = "oppression"
 wife of Machir of the tribe of Manasseh

A woman of the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.8.29; married to Abiel (H0022G); 
 mother of: Kish (H7027G), Ner (H5369G), Abdon (H5658J), Zur (H6698I), Baal (H1168B), Nadab (H5070J), Gedor (H1446I), Ahio (H0283I), Zecher (H2144), Mikloth (H4732G)
 § Maachah = "oppression"

A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Sa.27.2; 
 father of: Achish (H0397); also called Maacah (KJV: Maachah; NIV: Maakah) at 1Ki.2.39;
Another name of ma.okh (מָעוֹךְ "Maoch" H4582)
 § Maachah = "oppression"
 father of Achish, king of Gath at the beginning of Solomon's reign

A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.8; 
 son of: Koz (H6976); 
 brother of: Zobebah (H6637) and Harum (H2037) 
 § Anub = "confederate"
 son of Coz, descendant of Judah and Caleb through Ashur, the father of Tekoa
